      "writtenOn": "2024-02-12T19:16:59Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Heh, Skia doesn\u0027t even return a `size_t` like `fwrite` to indicate partial writes. So in practice `SkFILEWStream::write` already has the behavior that when returning false the buffer may have been partially written to the stream. So that\u0027s already in an undefined but destructable state. It seems unfortunate, but I suppose that\u0027s the precedent so far.",
      "parentUuid": "252b908e_3fd9e162",
      "revId": "967a5d1fb349795d891bfd681d41a31ab9f9ac17",
      "serverId": "5086850b-e599-37d2-8ec8-ff16aeccbf02"
    },
